<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:29Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Ukraine live: Romania probes possible drone attack on tanker</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77a38f576ae2de6e9cd1e4f7778c741c1a46d161184e8180305e1672be9a933f</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T03:52:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-ukraine-live-romania-probes-possible-drone-attack-on-tanker--ecf4ed2542dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261015-ukraine-live-romania-probes-possible-drone-attack-on-tanker" /><summary type="html">Romania on Wednesday was probing a possible fresh drone attack on a tanker off its Black Sea coast. Suspected Russian drones have hit several ships off Romania and neighbouring Bulgaria since last week in the latest spillover from the Ukraine war in the Black Sea. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Thousands protest across Colombia against new right-wing president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:04cd746ee6a79fe61655cc3dc245ee841becc0f21ade2e94782c33c6ba9632e5</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-15T01:57:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-thousands-protest-colombia-right-wing-president--3e6c97bc299e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261015-thousands-protest-colombia-right-wing-president" /><summary type="html">Thousands of Colombians protested peacefully across the country on Wednesday against right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella, in the opposition’s first major demonstrations since he took office in August. Former leftist President Gustavo Petro led a rally in Bogota, joined by trade unionists, Indigenous groups, students and feminist activists.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Lula’s party accuses Meta of election interference ahead of Brazil runoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff6a832e110b908b804bb8603eed6eef088f9b7efe9d611eab064fb37a07b856</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T23:52:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-lula-party-meta-election-interference-brazil-runoff--db9710e4afed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-lula-party-meta-election-interference-brazil-runoff" /><summary type="html">Brazilian President Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva’s party plans to file a complaint against Meta with the Organisation of American States, alleging election interference, his campaign said Wednesday. The party accuses Meta of restricting Lula’s online content ahead of the October 25 presidential runoff against Senator Flavio Bolsonaro. Meta denies the allegations.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>North Korea test-fires submarine-launched cruise missiles amid rising tensions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b87aa5f453fea5d112c0dad54a94b8bb7abe705a3d653ec0f06cf4d1c71c193e</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T23:12:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-north-korea-test-fires-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles--e31421af3b62.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261014-north-korea-test-fires-submarine-launched-cruise-missiles" /><summary type="html">North Korea test-fired two types of submarine-launched strategic cruise missiles on Wednesday, state media KCNA reported Thursday, saying the launches posed no threat to neighbouring countries. The tests follow heightened tensions with South Korea after a September 21 landmine explosion in the Demilitarised Zone injured three South Korean soldiers.</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Albania protests turn violent as protestors demand PM Rama's resignation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c4afafec5a6df71cb39eb8e2a1e8b77316852a6e64db0ec9cb2622a6068fe6fc</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:32Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T22:35:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-albania-protests-protestors-demand-pm-rama-resignation--fc3550df0859.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-albania-protests-protestors-demand-pm-rama-resignation" /><summary type="html">Anti-government protests in Albania’s capital Tirana turned violent for a second consecutive night on Wednesday, leaving several government buildings damaged and at least one ablaze. Thousands demanded Prime Minister Edi Rama’s resignation and improved university conditions. Police fired tear gas and deployed water cannons as protesters smashed windows and attacked buildings.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>PSG beat Manchester City in Champions League after financial rules verdict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00c97d11023c4007e47df4bedd8ea9805e460c2e54c67da7b52b167636365a57</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:35Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T21:48:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261014-psg-beat-manchester-city-champions-league--b99b22704b19.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261014-psg-beat-manchester-city-champions-league" /><summary type="html">Defending champions Paris Saint-Germain held off a second-half comeback to beat Manchester City 4-2 away in the Champions League on Wednesday. Goals from Desire Doue, Ousmane Dembele and Vitinha gave PSG a 3-0 lead before Erling Haaland struck twice. Maghnes Akliouche added a fourth, while Ferran Torres missed a late penalty.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>French anti-terror investigators probe True Crime Community link to school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1edf83528296ca3e667ad41f3e040c1d06f1742e8d68183553d8980e5cc79236</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:38Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T21:01:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261014-french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting--786227e648c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261014-french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting" /><summary type="html">The French anti-terrorism prosecutor has taken ​over the investigation into a school shooting near Marseille, after an initial probe found the 14-year-old suspect appeared to belong to ​a ‌group called the True Crime ⁠Community. Two teachers were shot and wounded, after a student opened fire with ⁠a hunting rifle that had been hidden inside a guitar case. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alexandre Rodde, security consultant, researcher and author of the report "Understanding nihilistic violent extremism and the True Crime Community in France".</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>French anti-terror investigators probe True Crime Community link to school shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f70e64e876560d03a7776a192aab43e60102c83715aa9e1b490e1c78e88b4b60</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:58:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting--965e949188ad.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-anti-terror-investigators-probe-true-crime-community-link-to-school-shooting" /><summary type="html">The French anti-terrorism prosecutor has taken ​over the investigation into a school shooting near Marseille, after an initial probe found the 14-year-old suspect appeared to belong to ​a ‌group called the True Crime ⁠Community. Two teachers were shot and wounded, after a student opened fire with ⁠a hunting rifle that had been hidden inside a guitar case. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Alexandre Rodde, security consultant, researcher and author of the report "Understanding nihilistic violent extremism and the True Crime Community in France".</summary></entry><entry><title>French glassmaker Duralex pulled back from the brink - again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:69d463e766c91bece7dc0fcb7a34754ea6befc8d8f3f0bd192f33ba9b9adf90c</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:55:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-glassmaker-duralex-pulled-back-from-the-brink-again--45a735744f12.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-glassmaker-duralex-pulled-back-from-the-brink-again" /><summary type="html">The French glassmaker Duralex is known for its practically unbreakable tableware - and business model. It's been pulled back from the brink for the fifth time in 25 years, by an entrepreneur who is vowing a new, environmentally-conscious chapter for the manufacturer. Also in the show - high energy prices fuel inflation in the US just weeks before midterm elections, and Greenland hits back at Donald Trump's plans for 'massive oil, gas, and mineral exploration' there.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya reports second Ebola case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbb0e0bd15637fa72021ad1af2455e0f32554b9f8f73f3651a9c3def20012c66</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/kenya-reports-second-ebola-case--4bbcfe9280cf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/kenya-reports-second-ebola-case" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Kenya confirms a second case of Ebola. Also, Nobel Peace Prize winner Navi Pillay warns that international justice is facing growing pressure. And millions of people in Nigeria have been without Tiktok for about a month.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>What is Starshield, SpaceX's military version of Starlink?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2f9710b969c2c8436702beff197b5fc727fe0b3aa0261104ab2bd17abecdce8</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:50Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T20:15:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-is-starshield-spacex-s-military-version-of-starlink--420f2336136c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261014-what-is-starshield-spacex-s-military-version-of-starlink" /><summary type="html">Elon Musk’s ⁠SpaceX restricted “military-grade” ​Starlink services overnight into Wednesday, hampering Ukrainian drone strike missions and air defenses, Ukraine reported. In response, Musk said that the US government was behind any slowdown in Ukraine's Starshield system.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Nord Stream may have been lawful target, argue lawyers for Ukrainian accused of bombing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6dd12fee8309636001c0b6c393844c951aef24a3cacfbd5ee3f957685600a47f</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:53Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:56:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing--ce42ad081609.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/nord-stream-may-have-been-lawful-target-argue-lawyers-for-ukrainian-accused-of-bombing" /><summary type="html">Lawyers for a Ukrainian ex-military officer accused of leading the bombing of Russia's Nord Stream ​pipeline in September 2022 argued at the start of his trial in Germany on Wednesday that "an aggressor's infrastructure" may have been a lawful target. FRANCE 24's Juliette Brown reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Starlink restriction 'no surprise' after Musk condemned Ukraine strikes on Russian data centres</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e7d3311bebc627ebfd979e43f4fd48eef8347cf534e4c77cc8a1a11673db2092</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:49:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres--fd09c9bb9e0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/starlink-restriction-no-surprise-after-musk-condemned-ukraine-strikes-on-russian-data-centres" /><summary type="html">Restrictions reported by Ukraine on its use of the US satellite internet system Starlink have exposed Kyiv's reliance on the technology for both offensive and defensive operations in its fight against Russia'a invasion, analysts and observers say. Speaking with FRANCE 24's Mark Owen, David Galbreath Professor of War and Technology at the University of Bath, says that "we always knew that allowing a private organisation like Starlink to have such a big impact on the combat operations in Ukraine was going to be challenging", explaining that "it is no surprise" that Starlink services had been throttled after SpaceX boss Elon Musk called the targeting by Ukrainian drones of data services in Russia "a step too far".</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump sparks outrage over AI tiger video after sharing footage of fatal UK attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9cf116f3fb7c8ddf069f7c61538c590031974337056fd17bcaa51110c3a84ca</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:54:59Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T19:39:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-outrage-over-ai-tiger-video-after-sharing-footage-of-fatal-uk-attack-1--f6bcc553bc17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-sparks-outrage-over-ai-tiger-video-after-sharing-footage-of-fatal-uk-attack-1" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump has sparked outrage after sharing the distressing footage of a 23-year-old man with mental illness being fatally mauled by a tiger at Yorkshire Wildlife Park, captioned "Don't ever mess with nature!" This followed hours later by an AI-generated video of himself taming a tiger. The posts have been condemned as disrespectful to the victim, William Chapman, and his grieving family, who have urged people to stop sharing harrowing content of the attack. Vedika Bahl goes through it.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>How far will cockroach movement go? India's youth-led protests defy Modi government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb56c417af0f1925f5e37cc336eb140d5ed948b2101984453e206e1627839db2</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:02Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T18:40:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government--26fd7d79299c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20261014-how-far-will-cockroach-movement-go-india-s-youth-led-protests-defy-modi-government" /><summary type="html">It all started as a bit of online satire by a few young people fed up by corruption. Clearly though, the Cockroach movement's no longer a laughing matter for India’s government which has shut transport and blocked rallying points in the capital to quell the momentum of youth-led mobilization that's already down the education minister over rampant school exam cheating and is now spearheading the protests against the culling of names from voter rolls, with the electoral commission chief accused of bias.</summary><category term="The Debate" /></entry><entry><title>‘Growing ambitions’: Dr. Kendall on Houthis’ quest to be recognised as Yemen’s ‘legitimate' leaders</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0e1cec7424a91a607dd6c6e560b031d4721e2240fc606d1db3551abd30e3c43c</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:05Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T17:18:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/growing-ambitions-dr-kendall-on-houthis-quest-to-be-recognised-as-yemen-s-legitimate-leaders--1fcca6275846.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/growing-ambitions-dr-kendall-on-houthis-quest-to-be-recognised-as-yemen-s-legitimate-leaders" /><summary type="html">What is the strategic logic behind the Houthis’ increasingly high-risk confrontation with Saudi Arabia? “Their experience in the past is that threats pay,” explains Dr. Elizabeth Kendall, Middle East specialist and President of Girton College, University of Cambridge. Dr. Kendall argues that the movement’s increasingly audacious military operations are not merely expressions of ideological hostility or Iranian influence, but calculated instruments of political coercion aimed at securing legitimacy, expanding territorial control and strengthening its negotiating leverage.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘The idea that Modi must be feared because he holds all levers of power has gone out of the window’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ffaa44440d4747b044014a27a45abf6b1ce5228bd4c5d258cd8e7b1bf170537d</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:08Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T16:51:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window--88dfae3f38b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-idea-that-modi-must-be-feared-because-he-holds-all-levers-of-power-has-gone-out-of-the-window" /><summary type="html">Is Narendra Modi losing his most powerful political asset: the perception of invincibility? As India's youth protest movement confronts an increasingly combative government, Dr. Subir Sinha, Director of the SOAS South Asia Institute and Reader in Development Studies, argues that the political significance of the demonstrations extends far beyond the arrests of opposition activists and the growing confrontation between protesters and state institutions. Dr. Sinha examines how the government's increasingly repressive response may be exposing the fragility of its authority and institutional legitimacy. Could India's emerging protest movement be dismantling the political mythology that has sustained Modi's hold on power?</summary></entry><entry><title>Houthis threaten escalation after strike on Saudi oil giant Aramco</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a36959e7d61122dac6117f35222c475214acccf2000fe736fb44f36300e05ca2</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:11Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T16:21:53Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261014-yemen-houthis-vow-continue-saudi-attacks-oil-giant-aramco-headquarters-hit--35d454874d36.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261014-yemen-houthis-vow-continue-saudi-attacks-oil-giant-aramco-headquarters-hit" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthi rebels said Wednesday they had targeted facilities belonging to Saudi oil giant Aramco after officials in Riyadh reported a strike on a building in an area housing the energy giant's headquarters. The Iran-back militia also claimed missile strikes on the capital Riyadh and vowed to continue attacking Saudi airports and oil facilities.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>In Phoenix, young ultra-conservatives look to carry on Charlie Kirk’s legacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f9ed815a3beaacee3bfbf2c976879ad40fa752f0fe8c52a9d2ecc23d15db43e</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:15Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:37:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-in-phoenix-young-ultra-conservatives-look-to-carry-on-charlie-kirk-s-legacy--b1cd212fca53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261014-in-phoenix-young-ultra-conservatives-look-to-carry-on-charlie-kirk-s-legacy" /><summary type="html">More than a year after the assassination of far-right influencer Charlie Kirk in September 2025, young activists from the organisation he co-founded, Turning Point USA, are working tirelessly to honour his legacy by rallying the youth vote ahead of the US midterm elections.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Houthis say targeted Saudi oil giant Aramco, vow more attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99623e2e8c158ce53051f717e8c964d83cc3e59ad15bb6ae3626b3941633ae0e</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:17Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T14:00:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-houthis-say-targeted-saudi-oil-giant-aramco-vow-more-attacks--6ecdaf15f5d6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-houthis-say-targeted-saudi-oil-giant-aramco-vow-more-attacks" /><summary type="html">Yemen's Houthis said Wednesday they had targeted facilities belonging to Saudi Aramco, after Saudi officials reported a strike on a building in an area housing the energy giant's operations centre. Powerful explosions meanwhile rattled the Saudi capital, as the coalition fighting the Houthis said it had intercepted a missile fired by the Iran-backed group towards Riyadh.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ceuta an 'inalienable' part of Spain, king says on key visit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4b175242a2d7e02a386be3f81c8ec5f1aeb597339e11873ba0479b1630113e79</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:20Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:58:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit--f40530a5a9e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ceuta-an-inalienable-part-of-spain-king-says-on-key-visit" /><summary type="html">King Felipe VI on Tuesday said Ceuta and Melilla were "an inalienable part" of Spain as he made a landmark visit to the north African territories claimed by neighbouring Morocco. But the monarch, who rarely makes political interventions, emphasised Spain's need to "maintain good neighbourly relations" with Rabat after July's unprecedented migrant surge into Ceuta strained historically delicate ties. FRANCE 24's Sarah Morris reports from Madrid, Spain.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ukraine accuses SpaceX of crippling military missions as ties with US worsen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:715bb0669bdf54875d7e24ad135f7ed38396c79dae6d9325f213195f63e25195</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:57:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ukraine-accuses-spacex-of-crippling-military-missions-as-ties-with-us-worsen--9bbce189de88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-ukraine-accuses-spacex-of-crippling-military-missions-as-ties-with-us-worsen" /><summary type="html">Ukraine accused Elon Musk's SpaceX on Wednesday of limiting Starlink services, crippling its drones, as Russian missiles knocked out power stations in attacks President Volodymyr Zelensky called "ostentatious disrespect" to Donald Trump. Kyiv's relationship with Washington has taken a sharp turn for the worse since US President Trump abruptly lifted sanctions on Russian diesel last week and publicly turned on Zelensky. FRANCE 24's Gulliver Cragg reports from Kyiv, Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>Cornell University bans fraternity parties after alleged gang rape</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9fb5030a660aa0f5449c07ad5a9924e38e80fdfda7015c2e3b3781272462ae3</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:26Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:55:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-cornell-university-bans-fraternity-parties-after-alleged-gang-rape--d3a9c6f05bea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-cornell-university-bans-fraternity-parties-after-alleged-gang-rape" /><summary type="html">Cornell University will ban parties and social events at fraternity houses until the end of the academic year, its president said on Tuesday, responding to the outcry over an alleged ​gang rape on ‌campus in 2024. The measure is the strongest reaction yet from Cornell's leadership to a lawsuit ⁠filed by a former undergraduate, Jane Doe, alleging seven men sexually assaulted her during a party. Over the last several weeks, the Ivy League school in Ithaca, New York, and its ‌president, Michael Kotlikoff, have come under heavy criticism over its response to ⁠the allegations.</summary></entry><entry><title>School closures persist in France as protests gain momentum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf36bb275e11b59f8c30d99fc9fae5e7b9096e802962c734297cc4e387e3bd31</id><updated>2026-10-15T04:55:29Z</updated><published>2026-10-14T13:53:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-school-closures-persist-in-france-as-protests-gain-momentum--b982e77c6975.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261014-school-closures-persist-in-france-as-protests-gain-momentum" /><summary type="html">Some high schools in France remained closed on Wednesday, a day after tens of thousands of people joined rallies across the country to support protesting students. On Saturday, national demonstrations against the spiralling cost of living are to take place, and unions and student groups see the two protest currents fusing together.</summary></entry></feed>
